# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore — production build context exclusions
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets, PHI-bearing runtime state, local tooling caches, and editor
# artifacts must never enter the image build context. The Dockerfile
# controls exactly what is COPY'd; this file keeps the context lean
# and prevents secret/PHI leakage into image layers or build cache.

# --- Git / version control ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# --- Dependencies & package-manager caches ---
node_modules/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/

# --- Secrets & environment files ---
# Real .env files and environment-specific secret files (.env.local,
# .env.production, ...) carry credentials and must never enter the build
# context. The tracked .env.example template is deliberately re-included
# via an explicit negation: it contains no secrets and stays available to
# the build; runtime secrets are delivered via a mounted .env, never baked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- PHI-bearing runtime state ---
# Clinical responses/requests, cursor, lock, audit, ledger, and the
# authenticated browser profile. Persistent state lives in a Docker
# named volume mounted at /app/.runtime — never baked into an image.
.runtime/

# --- Active configuration ---
# Contains real EHR URLs, captured PrognoCIS selectors, and org UUID.
# config/writeback.example.json and config/care1960-*.example.json are
# KEPT: they are synthetic, tracked, and used by the DRY validate:response
# run and tests.
config/writeback.json

# --- Local tooling / agent caches ---
.codex/
.playwright-cli/
.omo/

# --- Playwright artifacts from local test runs ---
playwright-report/
test-results/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# --- Editor / IDE ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.desktop.ini

# --- OS / log / temp artifacts ---
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.tmp
*.temp
.cache/

# --- Large tracked media (11.6 MB) that is never needed at build/runtime ---
nuance-dax-copilot-demo-video_67wDMgmL (1).mp3

# --- Captured payloads & docs (tracked, referenced only by README text) ---
# response.md is a captured API response file (may contain clinical sample
# data); docs/ holds the 458 KB architecture screenshot and guides. The
# Dockerfile copies only src/, test/, test-support/, and the synthetic config
# examples — these are excluded to keep the build context lean and free of
# payload data.
response.md
docs/